 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by a race condition in the `next()` method of `TicketSequence` where multiple threads could read the same value of `_next` without synchronization. The fix adds a lock around the read-modify-write operation to ensure thread-safe generation of unique ticket numbers. This guarantees that each thread receives a distinct ticket number even under concurrent access.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/sequence.py b/tracker/sequence.py\nindex 0cb5361..e4fbc06 100644\n--- a/tracker/sequence.py\n+++ b/tracker/sequence.py\n@@ -13,10 +13,10 @@ class TicketSequence:\n         self._next = value\n \n     def next(self):\n-        current = self._next\n-        self._store(current + 1)\n-        self.issued.append(current)\n-        return current\n-\n+        with self._lock:\n+            current = self._next\n+            self._store(current + 1)\n+            self.issued.append(current)\n+            return current\n     def peek(self):\n         return self._next\n",
